      "turn": 1,
      "user_message": "What is the maximum building height permitted in the HR-2 zone?",
      "assistant_text": "Based on my research, **the HR-2 zone does not have a single fixed maximum building height**. Instead, maximum building height in the HR-2 zone is determined by the **height precinct** that applies to the specific property, as mapped on **Schedule 15: Maximum Building Height Precincts**.\n\n## How Height Works in HR-2\n\nThe Regional Centre Land Use By-law uses a precinct-based system rather than zone-based height limits. Schedule 15 divides the Regional Centre into height precincts with varying maximum heights (examples from the bylaw include 8-metre, 11-metre, and taller precincts). The maximum height permitted on any HR-2 lot depends on which precinct that lot falls within.\n\n**Key provisions found:**\n- **Part V, Chapter 7** governs \"Built Form and Siting Requirements within the HR-2 and HR-1 Zones\"\n- **Section 200** addresses maximum streetwall heights in HR-2/HR-1, with provisions for buildings up to 6 storeys (streetwall equals building height) and taller than 6 storeys (streetwall capped at 6 storeys)\n- **Schedule 15** is the authoritative source for maximum building heights by precinct\n\n## To Get a Specific Answer\n\nYou need to identify the **height precinct** for your specific property. This requires either:\n1. Consulting Schedule 15 maps directly, or\n2. Providing a civic address so I can retrieve the applicable height precinct from the spatial dataset\n\nIf you have a specific property in mind, give me the address and I can tell you the exact maximum height permitted there along with the other envelope constraints (FAR, setbacks, streetwall).",
